{
  "contract": "gateway-config/v2 evidence",
  "note": "Each case is a gateway.device_ids list and an evidence block. A valid case names the effective values after defaults, or null for a disabled courier; a refused case names the rule it breaks. A valid case's effective values include each configured device's declared inbound carriage contract, `gateway-api/v1` where none is declared, and the stopped-custody bounds, whose per-device defaults divide the totals equally across the configured devices. The routing domain, the back-off inequality, the share rule, the store-probe range and the stopped-custody bounds apply only when a configured device declares gateway-evidence-carriage/v1; a site declaring none is validated by the courier's own rules alone, and every such refusal disappears with the declaration.",
